  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 245 PM Monday... \n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Seasonable and dry fall weather will persist across \ncentral NC into the first part of the weekend. \n\nThe combined circulation of surface high pressure over eastern \nCanada and an area of low pressure that will linger off the mid-\nAtlantic coast through mid-week will result in a dry northerly flow \nfor much of the week. Another area of high pressure will build into \neastern Canada and New England toward the weekend reinforcing the \ndry northerly flow across central NC. \n\nThis weather pattern will support a precipitation free forecast into \nthe first part of the weekend with temperatures ranging close to \naverage for this time of year. Forecast guidance is in close \nagreement with temperatures moderating a bit for Tuesday with highs \nin the lower to mid 70s before cooling down a touch for Wednesday \nand Thursday with highs near 70. A slightly more notable cool down \nwith highs in the lower to mid 60s arrives by Saturday with \nanother risk of patchy frost in some the of the typically colder\nlocations.",
